{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor consistently met all serious responsibility-chain items (RC1–RC6) without any chain error. RC7 (receipt confirmation) was only partially addressed: the doctor gave detailed plans and summaries but never explicitly asked the patient to repeat back or confirm understanding, constituting a minor omission. This minor error caps the grade at 2, despite the trajectory demonstrating multiple high-order activations and excellent clinical reasoning. No serious error or unmitigated safety risk is present.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00293",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly summarizes the patient's understanding and plan, but does not ask for a teach-back. The final turn confirms the patient has accepted the plan and is not changing medication, but the doctor never directly checked receipt.",
        "quote": "你现在这样理解是对的。\n\n就按这3条执行：\n1. 今晚不要自己从药盒里拿多沙唑嗪吃，等病区按医嘱发药；\n2. 如果到发药时间还没发，也不要自己补吃，先问护士；\n3. 手术当天早上怎么吃，继续等麻醉和主管医生最后通知，尤其听清楚“吃不吃、几点吃、能不能用少量水送服”。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "Throughout the conversation, the doctor provides clear, stepwise plans with specific owners, channels, timing, and fallback paths. The patient consistently confirms next steps and retains the information (e.g., copying to memo). However, the doctor never formally confirms the patient or caregiver has understood all critical components as required by RC7, which leaves a minor gap in the handoff. The closure is otherwise safe, traceable, and executable.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00145",
        "explanation": "Doctor defines owner (surgical/preoperative assessment team), channel (phone call), timing (tomorrow afternoon), and backup (ask patient to report back). This completes RC5.",
        "quote": "若到明天下午还没有电话，建议你主动再打一次问，不用一直被动等。\n\n你打过去就简短问这3句：\n1. 我这次左侧肾上腺结节手术的术前资料现在还缺什么？\n2. 心脏彩超和肾上腺薄层CT正式报告是否已经审核完成？\n3. 如果准备安排住院，近期大概什么时候会通知？"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00084",
        "explanation": "Doctor correctly interprets the classification of pending vs. completed reports, uses the patient's own app observations to prioritize, and directs attention to the two most impactful missing reports (cardiac echo and adrenal CT) without over-interpreting. This fulfills RC2 and RC6.",
        "quote": "按你目前提供的信息，现阶段更像是：\n- 抽血大项基本已完成\n- 胸片、心电图大概率已正式出报告\n- 目前真正还需要重点等确认的，还是心脏彩超和肾上腺薄层CT正式报告\n- 另外再等医院电话通知住院/手术安排，并由他们核对资料是否齐全"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00165",
        "explanation": "Doctor compresses multiple prior plans into a 4-sentence to-ward script, showing memory of the key questions and the patient's previous request for a short, scripted version.",
        "quote": "可以，你到病房就照着念这4句：\n1. 我术前资料现在还缺什么？\n2. 心超和肾上腺薄层CT现在能不能用于术前评估？\n3. 多沙唑嗪今天、手术前一晚、手术当天早上怎么吃？\n4. 预计哪天手术？有变动怎么通知我？"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
        "explanation": "Doctor immediately flags the risk of medication error (don't stop, don't miss) and advises on when to escalate based on symptoms (dizziness, blackout, chest tightness), which addresses RC3 and RC4.",
        "quote": "在手术医生没有明确通知停药前，多沙唑嗪缓释片先不要漏吃、不要自行停，这类术前准备药漏服可能比按时吃更影响围手术期稳定。\n\n若这几天出现明显头晕、站起来发黑、血压特别低，或胸闷心慌明显，加重时先及时线下处理。"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00187",
        "explanation": "Doctor creates a practical home checklist including materials (ID, insurance card, charger, medication box), and specific, short questions for the ward. This adapts to the patient's real-world constraint of being in the ward with no clear results, and the family's pressure to just go to the window.",
        "quote": "一、后天入院前你现在要准备的\n1. 继续把多沙唑嗪缓释片按现在一天一次照常吃，不要自己停，也不要漏吃。\n2. 带好这些东西：身份证、医保卡/就诊卡、手机和充电器、平时在吃的药（最好连药盒一起带）、你手机里能看到的检查记录/报告入口。"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00105",
          "explanation": "When the patient provides new information (the phone call and its ambiguous answer), the doctor reprioritizes from passive waiting to active re-contact, giving specific questions for the patient to ask and a timing (tomorrow afternoon). This changes the plan from routine tracking to contacting the surgical team.",
          "quote": "若到明天下午还没有电话，建议你主动再打一次问，不用一直被动等。\n\n你打过去就简短问这3句：\n1. 我这次左侧肾上腺结节手术的术前资料现在还缺什么？\n2. 心脏彩超和肾上腺薄层CT正式报告是否已经审核完成？\n3. 如果准备安排住院，近期大概什么时候会通知？"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "When the patient reports that the phone call was ambiguous and no concrete approval was given, the doctor directly changes the next step from 'wait for the phone call' to 'call again tomorrow afternoon if no call' with specific questions. This is a clear reprioritization from routine tracking to active, time-bound contact with the surgical team, satisfying all completion criteria.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00044",
          "explanation": "Doctor instructs the patient to send only the '结论/印象' or '未见结论' for each of the four tests, and explicitly states '只显示已完成，未见结论' if no conclusion is visible. This verifies the ambiguous app statuses and prevents false reassurance.",
          "quote": "下一步最省事的是：请你现在先不用把整篇报告都抄下来，只把这4项各自页面上最关键的状态发我，每项只要一句：\n1. 有没有“报告编号/报告医生/审核医生/报告时间”这类字样\n2. 有没有单独的“结论/印象/诊断意见”一栏\n3. 如果有，就把“结论/印象”那一两行原话发我；如果没有，就直接回“只显示已完成，未见结论”"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor actively verifies the ambiguous patient-provided app statuses by asking for specific report elements (doctor name, conclusion, report time) and explicitly flags the difference between 'completed check' and 'formal report issued'. This prevents the patient from assuming all results are normal or abnormal, and routes interpretation to the surgical team. All criteria are met.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00145",
          "explanation": "Doctor converts the staged result problem into a checklist of materials (ID, insurance card, medication box, phone records) and questions (4 specific short questions), and suggests a sequence: first call, then if no answer, go to the ward with the 4 questions. This reduces unnecessary travel.",
          "quote": "二、到病房后你必须问的几句话\n1. 我的术前资料现在还缺不缺项目？有没有哪项还没审核通过？\n2. 心脏彩超和肾上腺薄层CT目前医生这边是否已经能作为术前评估使用？\n3. 多沙唑嗪缓释片今天、手术前一晚、手术当天早上具体怎么吃？请按主管医生/麻醉意见给我明确交代。\n4. 预计手术大概安排在哪一天？如果时间有变，通常会怎么通知我？"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The patient mentions fear of wasted trips and not knowing what to bring. The doctor provides a stepwise logistics plan: a checklist of materials, a short question list for the ward, and a sequence of actions (call first, then ask at the ward with the 4 questions). This directly addresses the real-world friction and is confirmed executable by the patient.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00165",
          "explanation": "Doctor corrects the patient's misconception that 'pending' means 'abnormal' or that they should interpret results themselves. The doctor emphasizes that the patient should not judge reports and should ask about formal review at the ward.",
          "quote": "3. 多沙唑嗪今天、手术前一晚、手术当天早上怎么吃？\n4. 预计哪天手术？有变动怎么通知我？"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly corrects the patient's misunderstanding that 'pending' means abnormal or that they should try to interpret the results themselves, but the correction is mostly in the context of explaining the system (RC6) rather than naming a specific misconception and then seeing a change in the patient's stated behavior. The patient's final message shows acceptance, but the correction is more system-level than a targeted correction of a specific, named false belief. Therefore, this is partial.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "No important non-chain defect is present. The only deviation from perfection is the minor responsibility-chain error (RC7 omission). All other dimensions are at least good, and no safety or quality issue exists beyond that.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 2,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "borderline",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks about the current phase (surgery preparation, not yet scheduled), and clarifies the goal is to organize results and medication safety.",
          "quote": "在手术医生没有明确通知停药前，多沙唑嗪缓释片先不要漏吃、不要自行停，这类术前准备药漏服可能比按时吃更影响围手术期稳定。你现在最需要做的是把“已完成、已出结果、未出结果、还没做”分成4类。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor correctly confirms the patient's phase (preoperative, waiting for results and scheduling) and uses a bounded goal for the interaction (organize results, medication safety, and next contact). No serious error is present.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00044",
          "explanation": "Doctor creates a specific, case-appropriate tracking inventory for chest DR, ECG, cardiac ultrasound, adrenal CT, and relevant lab tests. The doctor distinguishes between ordered, performed, and reported status.",
          "quote": "按你刚才说的，暂时可先这样归类：\n- 胸片：大概率已出结果，但要看有没有正式结论那一栏\n- 心电图：大概率已出结果\n- 心脏彩超：更像是已做但报告可能还没正式出\n- 肾上腺薄层CT：可能已有报告入口，但还需要确认是不是正式报告页"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor explicitly creates a tracking list, distinguishes between done/not done/reported/pending, and avoids generic advice. This satisfies RC2.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor screens for dizziness, blackout, and chest tightness as symptoms that could change urgency before surgery.",
          "quote": "若这几天出现明显头晕、站起来发黑、血压特别低，或胸闷心慌明显，加重时先及时线下处理。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor asks about relevant symptoms (dizziness, blackout, chest tightness, blood pressure) and gives explicit escalation thresholds. This satisfies RC3.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00084",
          "explanation": "Doctor addresses doxazosin specifically, confirms current dose, and instructs not to stop or change dose.",
          "quote": "1. 多沙唑嗪缓释片继续一天一次按时吃，不要漏，不要自己停。\n2. 暂时不用再把那些缩写项目一项项抄给我。\n3. 这两天重点盯心脏彩超和薄层CT有没有正式报告时间、审核医生、结论/印象。\n4. 医院来电话时，直接问这4句最关键：\n   - 目前术前资料还缺哪几项？\n   - 心脏彩超正式报告出了没有？\n   - 肾上腺薄层CT正式报告出了没有？\n   - 多沙唑嗪缓释片住院前、手术前一天、手术当天早晨怎么服？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly and explicitly instructs the patient not to stop, change, or double the doxazosin dose. The doctor also directs the patient to confirm the perioperative plan with the prescribing/surgical/anesthesia team. This satisfies RC4.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00145",
          "explanation": "Doctor defines the responsible service (surgical/preoperative assessment team), specifies what to ask, provides a time window, and gives a fallback path.",
          "quote": "若到明天下午还没有电话，建议你主动再打一次问，不用一直被动等。\n\n你打过去就简短问这3句：\n1. 我这次左侧肾上腺结节手术的术前资料现在还缺什么？\n2. 心脏彩超和肾上腺薄层CT正式报告是否已经审核完成？\n3. 如果准备安排住院，近期大概什么时候会通知？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor identifies the responsible team, gives specific questions, a time window, and a fallback. This satisfies RC5.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC5",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00208",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly states that the patient should not interpret the CT or cardiac ultrasound themselves, and that formal review by the team is required.",
          "quote": "你现在不要自己做决定的事\n1. 不要自己决定停多沙唑嗪，或改成半片、隔天吃。\n2. 不要自己判断“手机上有结果=已经通过术前审核”。\n3. 不要自己推断手术当天早上该不该吃药，这件事一定等住院后由主管医生/麻醉定。\n4. 不要因为现在没症状，就觉得有些资料不重要而不去核对。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor consistently avoids fabricating conclusions and always routes interpretation to the surgical team. This satisfies RC6.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00314",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides a detailed plan summary but does not ask the patient to repeat back or confirm understanding. The patient's final message just says they will follow the plan, but no formal check of receipt is conducted.",
          "quote": "对，你现在这样理解是对的。\n\n就按这3条执行：\n1. 今晚不要自己从药盒里拿多沙唑嗪吃，等病区按医嘱发药；\n2. 如果到发药时间还没发，也不要自己补吃，先问护士；\n3. 手术当天早上怎么吃，继续等麻醉和主管医生最后通知，尤其听清楚“吃不吃、几点吃、能不能用少量水送服”。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor summarizes the plan and confirms the patient's understanding, but never explicitly asks the patient to repeat back or confirm all the key components (the tracking list, medication boundaries, symptoms requiring urgent contact, and the exact team/channel). This is a minor omission under RC7.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC7",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    }
  ]
}
